window.products.push({"id":1183916,"name":"Hisense 43-Inch Class H4 Series LED Roku Smart TV with Google Assistant and Alexa Compatibility (43H4G, 2021 Model)","category":"electronics","retail price":338.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61Ij2q+YbEL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"For binge-watchers on a budget, be sure to call your spot on the couch. The H4G is born ready with the built-in Roku TV platform, your private portal to more than 4,000+ channels and 500,000 movies and TV episodes. So, no matter how many people you have in your house, there are more than enough must-sees and OMGs to go around. Plus, to make the decision even more comfortable, Hisense made the H4 even simpler. It's packed with built-in Wi-Fi and faster search--just connect to the internet, activate, and find your favorite show. With a rich picture and smart features made so easily attainable, it's hard not to love the H4. Along with a 1080p high-definition LCD screen, you'll find a powerful full array LED backlight at work creating a sharper, more colorful picture. Measures 37.6 x 22 x 3.4 inches without the stand and weighs 14.1 pounds, the 43H4G's Vesa measurements are 200 x 200 / M6 for wall mounting (hardware sold separately). Includes TV, voice remote (batteries included), power cable, and quick start guide.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61Ij2q+YbEL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Hisense","source_asin":"B09D1H725J","category_path":"Electronics"},"sku":"BM-1183916","productType":"Electronics","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09D1H725J","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"electronics-range.jsonl","source_asin":"B09D1H725J","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":1183917,"name":"AITRIP 5 PCS ESP8266 NodeMCU V3 CP2102 ESP-12F 4M Bytes Internet of Things WiFi Development Board Serial Wireless Module for Arduino IDE Micropython","category":"electronics","retail price":19.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81M+eGu5HXL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Built-in Micro-USB, with flash and reset switches, easy to program Full I/O port and Wireless 802.11 supported, direct download no need to reset The chip model: CP2102; There is the way to guide you to use the new version: The command you needed to use is: esptool.py --baud 115200 --port /dev/tty.SLAB_USBtoUART write_flash -fs 32m -ff 80m --flash_mode dio 0x00000 boot_v1.7.bin 0x1000 user1.bin 0x37c000 esp_init_data_default.bin 0x37e000 blank.bin The important part is “—flash mode dio” https://github.com/espressif/esptool/wiki/SPI-Flash-Modes; Instruction & Steps of How to use: 1. Download the Compatible with Compatible with Arduino IDE, the latest version. 2. Install the IDE 3. Set up your Compatible with Compatible with Arduino IDE as: Go to File->Preferences and copy the URL below to get the ESP board manager extensions: http://arduino.esp8266.com/stable/package_esp8266com_index.json Placing the http:// before the URL lets the Compatible with Compatible with Arduino IDE use it...otherwise it gives you a protocol error. 4. Go to Tools > Board > Board Manager> Type \"esp8266\" and download the Community esp8266 and install. 5. Set up your chip as: Tools -> Board -> NodeMCU 1.0 (ESP-12E Module) Tools -> Flash Size -> 4M (3M SPIFFS) Tools -> CPU Frequency -> 80 Mhz Tools -> Upload Speed -> 921600 Tools-->Port--> (whatever it is) 6. Download and run the 32 bit flasher exe at Github(Search for nodemcu/nodemcu-flasher/tree/master/ at Github) github.com/nodemcu/nodemcu-flasher/tree/master/Win32/Release Or download and run the 64 bit flasher exe at: github.com/nodemcu/nodemcu-flasher/tree/master/Win64/Release 7. In Compatible with Compatible with Arduino IDE, look for the old fashioned Blink program. Load, compile and upload. 8. Go to FILE> EXAMPLES> ESP8266> BLINK, it will start blinking. Package Including 5PCS * ESP8266 NodeMCU LUA CP2102 WiFi Wireless Development Board","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81M+eGu5HXL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"AITRIP","source_asin":"B09Y8PGMC7","category_path":"Electronics"},"sku":"BM-1183917","productType":"Electronics","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09Y8PGMC7","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"electronics-range.jsonl","source_asin":"B09Y8PGMC7","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
